Z||000000||MooCow||09-16-2001||05:24 PM||||Is there a kit that has everything I need to install a complete suspension.  I am lost at what I need to buy since my car handles for crap.  I know my dogbone is shot and have one on the way.  I am going to just replace nearly the whole suspension, but dont know what I need.  I dont want to go all out cause I really dont race the car.  This is my daily driver car.<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||5
Z||000001||BlackDragon||09-16-2001||06:16 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A> <BR>koni racing suspension kit. rollbars springs shocks bushings. adjustable<BR>a little over $1000<P>------------------<BR>WTB:CHEAP black standard fiero. no engine is fine, any model/condition gray interior is a plus. must have title||||reg||1
Z||000002||SLYGUY||09-16-2001||07:21 PM||||I'm looking into suspension work for my car too. The only previous owner that this car has had screwed with the front end. Sucks. <P>He heated the springs in front. Thankfully not to much because it sits very nice and level. Not the lifted 4x4 look that is so very very common on all fieros, even the 88 with the redesign. I love how the car sits, but not so much how it rides. It rides okay, but you have to be careful with it. I've driven cars with modified suspension, even the cheap ineffective spring heating thing that were as low or lower than a fiero. <P>You can tell the moment that you sit in one that the whole car is very low, and this is confirmed the first time that you try and squeeze a floor jack and jackstands under it. I'm not sure if I like fieros lowered or not. It tends to make them porpous and bounce in front. Besides, the whole time you drive it you are bouncing around. As a kid this is a novelty and fun, but feels out of place in America's only mid-engined sports car.<P>I'm gonna have to decide if I want to replace the front springs to restore the orginal ride and that curb hopping 4x4 look or spend upwards of 2K to lower it professionally and change out the wheels and tires with 16-17" rims with low pro tires.<P>I haven't even found a set of wheels that I like better than the stock 88 GT 15 inchers that are on there now. I think they look best. Smooth, sleek, and sophisticated without the boy racer look or that you are trying to prove/say something.<P>Decisions Decisions.<P>I think I will stick with giving that sweet little V6 all that she needs/craves. Then the suspension thing. Did I mention that the stereo system has great potential?<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rick 88||09-16-2001||07:38 PM||||Moo Cow,<P>If you dog bone is shot check you motor and transmission mounts too. I had a broken foward transmission mount on my white 88 GT 5-speed and the car acted really wierd when you got on an off the throttle. I replaces all my mounts and dog bone and the car handled great.<P>Rick<BR>yelllow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||4
Z||000004||Oreif||09-16-2001||07:52 PM||||I ordered the KYB set-up from yhe Fiero Store. With the 10% discount it was only $650.00 with shipping. Not as adjustable as the KONI but handling is great.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
